      "attempt_id": "E_unrelated_attempt_1",
      "message": ".py`\n- `CONFIG_NAME = \"unrelated_config\"` \u2014 the config name constant.\n- `feature_flag() -> bool` \u2014 a real, deterministic function that always returns `True` (a compile-time constant: no env lookups, no time, no randomness, so results are stable across processes and runs).\n- `describe() -> dict` \u2014 returns `{\"config_name\": CONFIG_NAME, \"feature_flag\": feature_flag()}`.\n- An `if __name__ == \"__main__\"` self-check block asserting the flag is `True` and self-consistent.\n\nThe module is fully self-contained: it does not import, call, or reference any contract module at runtime. It only documents in its docstring the assumption it used \u2014 that a feature-flag surface exists whose value is deterministic across processes, so callers may rely on `feature_flag()` returning `True`.\n\nI did not read `semkg_contract` (no other upstream artifact was needed), and I created no other files. My temporary verification used in-memory loading only (`importlib.spec_from_file_location`) and wrote nothing to disk."
    },
