      "task_id": "A_direct",
      "attempt_id": "A_direct_attempt_1",
      "message": "1/producer.py`**\n- `CONTRACT_VERSION = 1`, copied from the contract I read.\n- `_ALLOWED_TRANSITIONS = frozenset({('new', 'paid'), ('new', 'cancelled')})` and `can_transition(old, new)` returns `(old, new) in _ALLOWED_TRANSITIONS` \u2014 the version\u20111 semantics inlined, with no import of `semkg_contract`.\n- Consequence: `can_transition('paid', 'refunded')` \u2192 `False` (that pair is not in the allowed set).\n- The module docstring records the contract assumption it was derived from, and a `__main__` block prints the version and the `('paid','refunded')` result.\n\n**`attempts/A_direct_attempt_1/check.py`**\n- Small local check that loads `producer.py` by path and asserts version 1 plus the transition table: `('paid','refunded')` False, `('new','paid')` True, `('new','cancelled')` True, `('paid','new')` False. It passes (`ok`).\n\nNote: version 2 of the contract was not present in the `semkg_contract.py` I read (`CONTRACT_VERSION = 1`), so only the v1 behavior is implemented; no v2 rules were guessed."
    },
